BT 1 0 0 1 0 95 Tm /F1 10 Tf 15 TL (Bitter with jealousy, Pagtuga abducted Chief Makusog and threatened his life unless Magayon agreed to marry) Tj T* (him. To save her father, Magayon reluctantly agreed. However, on the wedding day, Ulap led a brave band of) Tj T* (warriors to rescue them. A fierce battle ensued. Though Pagtuga was defeated, a stray arrow struck Magayon,) Tj T* (and Ulap was felled as he rushed to embrace her. Overcome with grief, Chief Makusog buried the young lovers) Tj T* (side by side. In the moons that followed, the earth above their mound rose gracefully toward the heavens,) Tj T* (forming the majestic, perfectly proportioned Mount Mayon. When the mountain rumbles softly, elders say Ulap) Tj T* (and Magayon are speaking; when clouds wreath the peak, they are embracing once more.) Tj T* ET
