BT 1 0 0 1 0 80 Tm /F1 10 Tf 15 TL (Across the archipelago, violent typhoons sweep over the islands with howling winds that snap ancient oaks and) Tj T* (uproot massive mahogany trees. Yet when the tempest subsides and the morning sun illuminates the drenched) Tj T* (countryside, one plant stands unbroken: the slender, humble bamboo. While mighty trees stubbornly oppose) Tj T* (the gale with brittle rigidity, the bamboo bends gracefully to the very earth, offering no futile defiance. It yields to) Tj T* (the tempest, waiting patiently until the storm has spent its fury, then springs back erect and triumphant toward) Tj T* (the sky.) Tj T* ET
