BT 1 0 0 1 0 50 Tm /F1 10 Tf 15 TL (In ancient times, the hawk and the hen were steadfast companions living peacefully in the forest. One day, the) Tj T* (hen wished to attend an aerial celebration across the valley, but she lacked the ability to soar above the tree) Tj T* (canopy. The generous hawk lent her his cherished copper wing-ring, cautioning her: 'Guard this talisman with) Tj T* (your life; it was bestowed upon my lineage by our ancestors.') Tj T* ET
