BT 1 0 0 1 0 65 Tm /F1 10 Tf 15 TL (While dancing joyfully, the careless hen loosened the ring, and it vanished into the tall grass. Ashamed and) Tj T* (anxious, she searched day and night but could not recover it. When the hawk returned and discovered her) Tj T* (negligence, he declared: 'Until you restore my ancestral ring, you and all your descendants shall scratch the) Tj T* (earth in eternal search, and I shall claim your chicks as payment for your broken trust.' To this very day, hens) Tj T* (unceasingly scratch the soil looking for the lost talisman, while hawks circle vigilantly from the clouds above.) Tj T* ET
